# Python rules

## Style

- Python 3.11+, `from __future__ import annotations` in new modules
- Ruff for format/lint; mypy strict — type all public functions
- Pydantic v2 models for domain objects (Run, Step, EvalResult, ReleaseDecision)
- snake_case functions, PascalCase classes, UPPER_SNAKE constants

## Patterns

```python
# Prefer pure functions + injected deps
def evaluate_run(run: Run, registry: EvaluatorRegistry) -> list[EvalResult]: ...

# Severity must be explicit
severity: Literal["info", "warning", "major", "critical"]
```

## Avoid

- Bare `except:`, untyped public APIs, `print()` in library code
- LangGraph/LangChain imports outside `adapters/`
- God files >400 lines — split by responsibility
- Live LLM calls in default unit tests

## Tests

- pytest in `tests/` mirroring module structure
- `@pytest.mark.integration` for network/API tests
- Golden cassettes in `tests/fixtures/`
